  "_doc": "Security C1 (single source, RULE 30). E2E_PREF and E2E_PREF_REFUSED are RELAY-MINTED frames; a peer socket that sends them is impersonating the relay and the relay drops them before any forward, listener mirror, resume passthrough or resume buffer. `prefixes` is the relay's exact, case-sensitive raw-string prefix list (server.js RELAY_OWNED_PREF_FRAME_PREFIXES). Clients split the type at the FIRST ':' with no trim and no case folding, so the near-miss rows are frames no client would dispatch as E2E_PREF and the relay forwards them like any other data frame. Consumers: tests/relay-e2e-pref-frame-filter.test.mjs (node) and the Kotlin twin on the android lane. from: phone | browser | listener. pairState: active (sender is the active peer), listener-mirror (phone is active, a passive extension listener sits in the lobby), resume (sender is in the lobby, the opposite peer is a soft-held survivor under an armed claim), resume-reform (as resume, and the claim re-forms the pair on this frame), resume-buffer (lobby phone, no survivor, armed claim). expect: dropped | forwarded (forwarded under resume-buffer means buffered for replay).",
